#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:986
msgid ""
"When submitting a PR, it is highly recommended that all modifications are "
"thoroughly tested. This is further enforced in the CI by the `codecov GitHub"
" action <https://app.codecov.io/gh/pyvista/pyvista>`_ which has a 90% "
"target, that is, it ensures that 90% of the code modified in the PR is "
"tested. It should be mentioned that branch coverage is measured on the CI, "
"meaning for examples that both values of an ``if`` clause must be tested to "
"ensure full coverage. For more details on branch coverage, please refer to "
"the `coverage documentation "
"<https://coverage.readthedocs.io/en/latest/branch.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:993
msgid ""
"If needed, code coverage can be deactivated for specific lines by adding the"
" ``# pragma: no cover`` or ``# pragma: no branch`` comments. See the "
"documentation `excluding code "
"<https://coverage.readthedocs.io/en/latest/branch.html#excluding-code>`__ "
"for more details. However, code coverage exclusion should rarely be used and"
" has to be carefully justified in the PR thread if no simple alternative "
"solution has been found."
msgstr ""
"必要であれば、 ``# pragma: no cover`` または ``# pragma: no branch`` "
"のコメントを追加することで、特定の行のコードカバレッジを無効にすることができます。詳しくは `excluding code "
"<https://coverage.readthedocs.io/en/latest/branch.html#excluding-code>`__ "
"を参照してください。しかし、コードカバレッジの除外はめったに使うべきでなく、簡単な代替案が見つからない場合は、PRスレッドで注意深く正当化しなければなりません。"

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1000
msgid "Test Code Is Covered Too"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1002
msgid ""
"``tests`` is measured alongside ``pyvista``, and the two are uploaded to "
"Codecov as separate reports under the ``package`` and ``tests`` flags, so a "
"gain on one cannot hide a loss on the other. New and changed test code must "
"be fully covered, and the total may not fall: an uncovered line in a test "
"file is a test that does not run the code it appears to, and a partly "
"covered branch is a case the suite never reaches. Both usually mean a "
"missing assertion rather than a missing ``pragma``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1009
msgid ""
"Reach for ``# pragma: no cover`` when a branch exists in order to prove it "
"is never taken -- a callback asserted never to fire, a fallback for a "
"backend no covered environment runs -- and say which in the comment. ``# "
"pragma: no branch`` fits a loop or guard that only ever goes one way, such "
"as a retry loop whose last attempt always returns or raises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1014
msgid "Some patterns produce dead test code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1016
msgid ""
"A helper class or fixture whose attributes nothing ever reads. Delete the "
"unused member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1017
msgid ""
"A stub body written as ``class Stub: ...``. Coverage counts the one-line "
"form as a partial branch, and ``ruff format`` collapses ``...`` onto the "
"``class`` line, so write ``pass`` or a docstring instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1020
msgid ""
"A no-op callback whose body is ``pass`` or a bare ``return``, registered "
"somewhere that never calls it. Give it a docstring instead and delete the "
"statement: a docstring is not an executable line, so nothing is left to go "
"uncovered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1023
msgid ""
"A class registered or patched but never instantiated, where ``__init__`` "
"only assigns. Drop the ``__init__``, or assert on the instance the test "
"already set up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1025
msgid ""
"A branch that only one CI job reaches. Coverage is combined across the "
"matrix, so a ``vtk_version_info`` gate is covered as long as some job takes "
"each side. Only the Linux jobs upload, so a ``sys.platform`` gate for macOS "
"or Windows never is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1029
msgid ""
"Not every file under ``tests`` is measured. The ones run outside a ``-cov`` "
"environment (the ``doc_build`` suite, the standalone scripts, the Sphinx "
"projects used as build fixtures) are listed under ``report.omit`` in "
"``pyproject.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1033
msgid ""
"The CI is configured to test multiple vtk versions to ensure sufficient "
"compatibility with vtk. If needed, the minimum and/or maximum vtk version "
"needed by a specific test can be controlled with a custom pytest marker "
"``needs_vtk_version``, enabling the following usage (note the inclusive and "
"exclusive signs):"
msgstr ""
"CIは、vtkとの十分な互換性を確保するために、複数のvtkバージョンをテストするように構成されています。必要であれば、特定のテストが必要とする vtk"
" の最小および/または最大のバージョンをカスタム pytest marker ``needs_vtk_version`` で制御することができます "
"(包括的および排他的符号に注意):"

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1070
msgid "Testing Against VTK Master"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1071
msgid ""
"Most unit testing is run against stable VTK releases. However, when "
"developing features that depend on upstream VTK changes or when "
"investigating regressions, it can be useful to test against the latest VTK "
"development code. VTK publishes development wheels to the VTK wheels index, "
"which are snapshots of recent development builds. To install them locally, "
"run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1080
msgid ""
"For pull requests, applying the ``vtk-dev-testing`` label enables an "
"additional CI job that installs these development wheels and runs the unit "
"test suite against them. Although these wheels are official VTK builds, they"
" are only published periodically (typically once per week) and may not "
"include the latest commits from the VTK repository. As a result, passing "
"``vtk-dev-testing`` does not guarantee compatibility with the current VTK "
"master branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1085
msgid ""
"To test against the very latest upstream VTK source, apply the ``vtk-master-"
"testing`` label instead. This enables a CI job that clones the VTK "
"repository, builds VTK directly from the current master branch, and runs the"
" unit tests against that build. This provides the most up-to-date "
"compatibility testing and is recommended when changes depend on recent VTK "
"development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1090
msgid ""
"The ``vtk-dev-testing`` and ``vtk-master-testing`` labels are independent "
"and may be applied separately or together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1094
msgid ""
"The PR either needs a new commit, for example updating the branch from "
"``main``, or to be closed/re-opened to rerun the CI with the label applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1098
msgid "Testing Against the ``cvista`` Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1099
msgid ""
"PyVista also runs against `cvista <https://github.com/pyvista/cvista>`_, a "
"community fork of VTK. Stock VTK is the default and is tested on every PR; "
"cvista is tested at **integration cadence**—nightly, and on PRs carrying the"
" ``integration-testing`` label:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1107
msgid ""
"It is not on the per-PR fast path because it is a full extra run of the "
"suite against a second VTK build, and because a failure there is rarely a "
"reason to block an unrelated PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1110
msgid ""
"**When the suites disagree, fix cvista.** PyVista is not held back by the "
"fork: if a change here is correct against stock VTK but fails on cvista, the"
" fix belongs upstream in cvista, not in a marker or an ignore list here. "
"Open an issue on `pyvista/cvista "
"<https://github.com/pyvista/cvista/issues>`_ and keep going."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1114
msgid ""
"The ``skip_vtk_backend`` marker is only for **permanent, by-design** "
"divergence—a module the fork does not build, or behaviour that differs "
"deliberately. Attach it to the test with a reason naming the specific cause:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1125
msgid ""
"It is not a way to park a real regression. In library code, use "
":func:`pyvista.vtk_backend` to raise a clear error for a build that cannot "
"support a feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1129
msgid "Garbage Collection Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1130
msgid ""
"Every test is checked for reference leaks: no plotter or VTK object created "
"by a test may outlive it. The autouse ``check_gc`` fixture in "
"``tests/conftest.py`` covers the whole repository, and "
"``tests/plotting/conftest.py`` overrides it with a version that also watches"
" plotters. A leaking test fails at teardown with a rendered chain of what "
"still holds a reference; see the `refleak <https://github.com/mne-"
"tools/refleak>`_ documentation for how to read it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1137
msgid ""
"The check freezes the heap rather than scanning it, so it costs no "
"measurable time and every CI job runs it. ``--no_check_gc`` turns it off for"
" a whole run, for local iteration where the report is in the way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1145
msgid ""
"The cause of a leak is usually a reference cycle, and fixing it (for "
"example, with :mod:`weakref`) is preferred over silencing the check with "
"either of these markers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1163
msgid ""
"``expect_check_gc_fail`` outranks ``--no_check_gc``, so the tests that "
"exercise the check itself (``tests/core/test_gc.py``, "
"``tests/plotting/test_gc.py``) cannot pass while nothing is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1168
msgid "Docstring Testing"
msgstr "Docstringテスト"

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1169
msgid "Run all code examples in the docstrings with:"
msgstr "docstring内のすべてのコード例を実行します．"

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1197
msgid ""
"``make doctest`` runs ``tox run -f doctest``, which runs both the ``doctest-"
"modules`` environment above and the ``doctest-names`` environment (``tox run"
" -e doctest-names``). The latter has no ``pytest`` equivalent since it does "
"not run the examples: it statically checks that the names they use are "
"actually defined (see ``tests/check_doctest_names.py``). Pass "
"``ARGS=\"-v\"`` to list every docstring as it is checked. CI runs the two as"
" separate jobs in ``.github/workflows/style-docstring.yml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1208
msgid ""
"Additional testing is also performed on any images generated by the "
"docstring. See `Documentation Image Regression Testing`_."
msgstr ""
"また、docstringによって生成された画像に対しても追加のテストが行われる。 詳しくは `ドキュメント画像の回帰テスト`_ を参照のこと。"

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1213
msgid "Type Checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1214
msgid ""
"PyVista uses `mypy <https://mypy.readthedocs.io/>`_ for static type "
"checking. Configuration lives in the ``[tool.mypy]`` section of "
"``pyproject.toml``. ``-n 2`` checks with two worker processes, as the "
"``tox`` environment does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:0
msgid "mypy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1244
msgid "Typing Tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1245
msgid ""
"Mypy only sees the annotations, so a hint can be wrong without Mypy "
"noticing: the annotated type and the type a function actually returns may "
"disagree, and complex ``@overload`` definitions may not resolve to the "
"overload they were meant to. The typing tests pin both halves, so a mismatch"
" between them fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1250
msgid "Install the regular test requirements with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1256
msgid "The tests can be executed with:"
msgstr "テストは次のようにして実行することができます:"

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1283
msgid "Writing a Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1284
msgid ""
"Cases live in ``tests/typing/cases``, under ``core`` or ``plotting`` after "
"the subpackage of the callable they exercise. A case is one line: an "
"expression, and the type it should have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1294
msgid ""
"``assert_types`` comes from `type-assert <https://github.com/user27182/type-"
"assert>`_ and is two things at once. To Mypy it is "
"`typing_extensions.assert_type <https://typing-"
"extensions.readthedocs.io/en/latest/#typing_extensions.assert_type>`_, which"
" requires the expression's inferred type to match the second argument "
"*exactly*: a supertype is a failure, not a pass. At runtime it is a checker "
"that inspects the value the expression actually produced. Writing the type "
"once is enough for both, and a case only passes if the two agree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1302
msgid ""
"Write the expected type as an ordinary expression, such as ``pv.PolyData``, "
"``pv.PolyData | pv.ImageData``, ``list[tuple[str, DataSet]]``, rather than "
"as a string. Anything in the file that is not an ``assert_types`` line is "
"setup: imports, and helpers such as the ``multi()`` above that builds a "
"fresh ``MultiBlock``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1307
msgid ""
"Each file holds the cases of one callable and is named after it: "
"``clip_scalar.py``, ``principal_axes.py``. A method takes its class as a "
"lowercase prefix only when the bare name would not identify it, as for "
"dunders (``multiblock_getitem.py``, ``multiblock_setitem.py``) and names "
"that several classes share (``transform_apply.py``). A file carries all the "
"setup it needs, even when another file has the same helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1313
msgid ""
"The directory carries its own ``ruff.toml`` raising the line length, so a "
"case stays on one line however long it gets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1317
msgid "How the Cases Run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1318
msgid ""
"Each case file is collected as a test file of its own. Every case in it "
"becomes one runtime test and one static test per configured checker, named "
"after the claim it makes rather than after where it sits in the file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1327
msgid ""
"The runtime half compiles the file's setup, runs it in a namespace of its "
"own and then executes that one case against it, so a case cannot reach "
"another case's state and reordering a file changes nothing. It walks "
"containers exhaustively, so it catches a ``None`` at any position in a "
"``list[DataSet]``, not only the first element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1333
msgid ""
"The static half reads a single Mypy run, made once per session in a separate"
" process, and reports the diagnostics landing on that case's lines. Mypy "
"failing to run fails only these tests. Lines that are not cases are covered "
"by a ``setup`` test, one per file, so a broken import reads as a broken "
"import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1339
msgid "Skipping a Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1340
msgid ""
"A case that cannot run everywhere, because it crashes a platform or needs a "
"dependency that is not always present, is named in a ``SKIP_RUNTIME`` "
"mapping in its own file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1350
msgid ""
"Only the runtime half is skipped; Mypy still checks the case. The mapping is"
" read after the file's setup has run, so making an entry conditional is "
"ordinary Python. An entry naming an expression that no case makes fails the "
"``setup`` test, so a skip cannot quietly outlive the case it was written "
"for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1356
msgid "The Framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1357
msgid ""
"The machinery lives in `type-assert <https://github.com/user27182/type-"
"assert>`_, a standalone package that knows nothing about PyVista. It "
"registers itself as a pytest plugin and takes one setting in "
"``pyproject.toml``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1365
msgid ""
"That setting sits in the shared ``[tool.pytest.ini_options]``, and unknown "
"options are errors, so the package belongs in every dependency group whose "
"environment runs pytest against this configuration, not only the ones that "
"run the typing tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1370
msgid ""
"The checkers it drives are selectable with ``type_assert_checkers``, which "
"defaults to Mypy and accepts more than one. Report anything wrong with the "
"framework itself against that repository rather than this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1375
msgid "Documenting Type Aliases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1376
msgid ""
"The documentation expands a type alias into its full value wherever it "
"appears in a signature. To show and link an alias by name instead, which "
"suits long unions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1379
msgid ""
"Export it from ``pyvista/typing/__init__.py`` and add it to that module's "
"``__all__``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1380
msgid "Add its name to ``_DOCUMENTED_TYPES`` in ``doc/source/conf.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1381
msgid "Document it in ``doc/source/api/core/typing.rst``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1383
msgid ""
"Docstrings can then refer to the alias by its bare name, for example "
"``center : VectorLike[float]``, and the documentation build reports a broken"
" link to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1387
msgid ""
"A name that appears in a signature but has no documentation page, such as a "
"private ``TypeVar``, fails the documentation build. Add it to "
"``_UNDOCUMENTED_TYPES`` in ``doc/source/conf.py``, keeping the list sorted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1391
msgid ""
"If the name belongs to another package whose documentation Sphinx links to, "
"such as ``Path`` from ``pathlib``, map it to its full name in "
"``_REFERENCE_NAMES`` instead, so it links rather than being ignored."
msgstr ""

